.TH GALTERNATIVES 1 "2026-11-01" "galternatives" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
galternatives \- graphical configuration tool for the alternatives system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B galternatives
.RI [ option ...]
.RI [ group ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B galternatives
provides a graphical interface to
.BR update-alternatives (1).
It lets users choose the default program for commands managed by the
alternatives system.
It also supports adding, editing, and removing alternative groups and options,
and working with a custom alternatives database.
.PP
The optional
.I group
argument must name an existing alternative group.
At most one group may be specified.
.PP
By default, changes made by an ordinary user are submitted through
.BR pkexec (1)
for authorization.
Use
.B \-\-normal
to run commands with the current user's privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Show all command-line options, including GTK and GApplication options, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-normal
Run without requesting additional privileges through
.BR pkexec (1).
This option does not change the privileges of a process already running as root.
.TP
.BI \-\-altdir " directory"
Use
.I directory
for alternative symlinks instead of
.IR /etc/alternatives .
.TP
.BI \-\-admindir " directory"
Read and update alternative group state files in
.I directory
instead of
.IR /var/lib/dpkg/alternatives .
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Write the
.BR update-alternatives (1)
log to
.I file
instead of
.IR /var/log/alternatives.log .
.SH NOTES
Before version 1.0.12,
.B galternatives
interpreted
.B \-\-altdir
and
.B \-\-admindir
in reverse.
These options now have the same meanings as in
.BR update-alternatives (1).
